.save all
.probe alli
* This relaxes the simulation accuracy so it converges easier, 
* see [this post](https://forum.kicad.info/t/timestep-too-small-is-killing-me/44015/9)
.options method=gear chgtol=1e-11 reltol=0.1 rshunt=1G rseries=0.05 cshunt=1p abstol=1n vntol=0.1m trtol=1
******************************

.control
* wait until simulation has finished:
set controlswait
tran 25n 79.2u 25n
* set ouput format for cvs:
set wr_vecnames
set wr_singlescale
* option numdgt=7
* data to csv file:
* The following lines are used to write all circuit nodes in a .txt file as simulation output. All final nodes include ReRAM internal states, and they are used to initialize the circuit for next operation (initial conditions required for differential equations).
